// The watchman keeps to his own rounds: an NPC composing only
// `sprout.Actor`, who follows whoever leaves the yard out through its
// one exit, exactly as a visitor's own `go` would (the spec's Verbs ›
// Acting). The shed has no way back, so once he is in it he stays. The
// crow makes the same crossing on the yard's own tick, naming the shed
// itself rather than a message's bound parameter.
world rounds is sprout.World {
  visitors are Person
  visitors arrive at yard

  object yard is Yard {
    grammar { exit in "in through the low door" -> shed }
    object watchman is Watchman
    object crow is Crow
  }

  object shed is sprout.Place
}
